      <h3>Options</h3>
      <div class="options-grid">
        <section class="option">
          <h4>A. Require Python 3.10 or newer</h4>
          <p>Add one prerequisite line to <code>sample/QUICKSTART.md:1</code>. <code>sample/hello.py:3-7</code> stays as is.</p>
          <p>Tradeoff: no code change, but Python 3.9 users still can't run the sample.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="option">
          <h4>B. Make the sample work on Python 3.9</h4>
          <p>Replace the <code>match</code> block at <code>sample/hello.py:3-7</code> with an if/else over <code>sys.argv[1:]</code>.</p>
          <p>Tradeoff: runs on 3.9 and later, but changes the sample's code.</p>
        </section>
      </div>

      <div class="decision">
        <p>The human wrote “ok go ahead with the fix”. The maintainer asked which option. The human replied “approve B”.</p>
        <p class="approval-stamp">APPROVED · B · 07:35 UTC</p>
